      "review": {
        "date": "2026-10-15",
        "notes": "Author-written, modelled on the 3.5 product-rule-with-trig exercises (e.g. 177, 181). Product rule: (x^2)'cos x + x^2 (cos x)' = 2x cos x - x^2 sin x, so a. Distractors: b flips the sign of (cos x)'; c is (x^2)'(cos x)' = -2x sin x; d drops the x^2 (cos x)' term. Each is genuinely wrong, e.g. at x = pi/2: y' = -pi^2/4, b = +pi^2/4, c = -pi, d = 0. SymPy confirmed a equals y' and b, c, d do not.",
