      "review": {
        "date": "2026-10-15",
        "notes": "Product rule with u = x + cos x, v = 1 - sin x: u' = 1 - sin x, v' = -cos x. dy/dx = (1 - sin x)(1 - sin x) + (x + cos x)(-cos x) = (1 - sin x)^2 - cos x (x + cos x), matching the OpenStax answer key for 181. Domain: all reals (only sin, cos and polynomials). Cross-checked with a throwaway SymPy diff/simplify. LaTeX puts the cos x factor last: Compute Engine parses \\cos x\\,(x+\\cos x) as cos(x(x + cos x)).",
